    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="1450" n="1336" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">On the Train</hi>, <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quebec</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-13">September 13,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Franklin</hi>, I send you herewith a number
                    of notes and telegrams which I have prepared, arising out of our talks
                    yesterday. These include a telegram to U.J.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d648-f1"/> which, as it mentions your
                    affairs, I <pb facs="1451" n="1337" xml:id="pg1337"/> have asked my Government
                    to hold till I get your okay with any alterations.</p>
                <p>We have all greatly enjoyed this trip, and I cannot tell you what a pleasure it
                    has been to me, to Clemmie and to Mary to receive your charming hospitality at
                    the White House and at Hyde Park. You know how I treasure the friendship with
                    which you have honoured me and how profoundly I feel that we might together do
                    something really fine and lasting for our two countries and, through them, for
                    the future of all.</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">inston</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Churchill</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>








